#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0370 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "[STALE MECHANISM, corrected 2026-08-27] NonEmptyGuardInliner was DELETED (Fix #367 / EC-100) and no guard is injected at load any more; the expectation below still holds, but for the rule's AUTHORED Requirements/Check, not for the injection this note describes. THE 82-RULE GENERATOR-WILDCARD POPULATION (Fix #331 finding; owner ruled 2026-08-22 that all 82 are BUCKET 1 - no rule edit - with a sample of fixtures owed by the closing lane; authored by Fix #340). These rules never carried the injected var_exists guard in rules/ (NonEmptyGuardInliner.isGeneratorWildcard excludes wildcard names), but WildcardExpander re-ran installNativeExpr on the EXPANDED rule, where the arm wrapped the now-concrete leaf - so before Fix #330 an absent primary column silenced them at runtime. With the arm retired the expanded leaf is a bare empty(X): absent = all-missing, TRUE on every row. ATMF is the only column matching any of the three patterns, so there is EXACTLY ONE expansion (root 'A'); ATM and ADTM are both synthesised absent, empty() is TRUE on both, and row 1 fires. Row 2 leaves ATMF blank and stays silent. Any extra column ending in TM/TMF/DTM would add an expansion and change the count - the column list is load-bearing."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 ATMF=T
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col ATMF    type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | T
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | ALB |
---
